# Smatchet project rules

The canonical Smatchet project rules, agent delegation table, semantic-codebase-search policy, self-improvement loop, and harness-adapter section all live in **[`AGENTS.md`](../AGENTS.md)** at the repo root.

This file exists only so Claude Code (which auto-loads `.claude/CLAUDE.md`) picks up AGENTS.md content. The `@`-import below is Claude Code's file-include syntax — other agentic harnesses read `AGENTS.md` directly per the [agents.md spec](https://agents.md/).

@../AGENTS.md


## Codebase navigation — semantic search + grep

AGENTS.md § Semantic codebase search says *navigate by meaning before raw
text-search*. On Claude Code the concrete tools are vexp `run_pipeline`
(graph-ranked context, when its daemon is up) and `Grep`/`Glob`
(literal/symbol sweeps). The former Sourcetrail `st_query.py` rung is
retired — upstream discontinued, and its prebuilt symbol DB never existed
in a fresh checkout.

### Grep / Glob — literal & exhaustive sweeps
Use `Grep`/`Glob` for exhaustive literal/symbol inventories and mechanical
rename sweeps (every occurrence must be found — graph queries are not
exhaustive), and as the fallback when semantic search is unavailable.

### Subagent / Explore / Plan mode
- Subagents may call grep directly — pass the task description.
- Reserve Agent(Explore) for broad fan-out; a targeted Grep answers a
  single "who calls X / where is X" question more cheaply.